[0.003, "o", "\u001b[34;1H\u001b[38;5;248m\u001b[48;5;255m\u276f \u001b[38;5;16mOK let's try to get some testing and eval infrastructure in place. You can add that sample test image to the repo, \u001b[39m   \u001b[35;1H  \u001b[38;5;16mand also put it in some test data directory. Then let's get a test harness in place to check its contents against \u001b[39m    \u001b[36;1H  \u001b[38;5;16msome known-good data. Get that in place and I can manually check it against the image\u001b[39m                                 \u001b[37;3H\u001b[49m    \u001b[C          \u001b[C     \u001b[C   \u001b[C    \u001b[C  \u001b[C     \u001b[C   \u001b[C \u001b[C   \u001b[C        \u001b[C     \u001b[C  \u001b[C       \u001b[C   \u001b[C      \r\n\u001b[38;5;174m\u00b7\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;174mJitterbugging\u2026 \u001b[39m                                                                                                       \u001b[39;1H\u001b[38;5;241m  \u23bf \u00a0\u001b[39m\u001b[40;120H\n\u001b[38;6H\u001b[38;5;241mTip: Use /config to change your default\u001b[Cpermission mode (including Plan Mode)\u001b[39m\u001b[40;1H\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;246m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500"]
