[0.003, "o", "\u001b[32;1H\u001b[38;5;248m\u001b[48;5;255m\u276f \u001b[38;5;16mEh stop for now. I don't want to dive into that. Let's first deal with this business of how to manage the failure we \u001b[39m \u001b[33;1H  \u001b[38;5;16mjust saw. IMO it's \u201cgood enough\u201d on the item names. The difference in null/subtotal behavior is a little weird.\u001b[39m       \u001b[34;1H                                                                                                                        \u001b[35;1H  \u001b[38;5;16m1. Why did those three things happen (the null behavior for date, for \"Unexpected\", for subtotal?\u001b[39m                     \u001b[36;1H  \u001b[38;5;16m2. Can we do some fuzzy matching to say those names are OK?\u001b[39m                                                           \u001b[37;3H\u001b[49m  \u001b[C   \u001b[C  \u001b[C  \u001b[C    \u001b[C     \u001b[C        \u001b[C  \u001b[C   \u001b[C     \u001b[C     \u001b[C   \u001b[C    \r\n\u001b[38;5;174m\u2736\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;174mComputing\u2026 \u001b[39m                                                                                                           \u001b[39;1H\u001b[38;5;241m  \u23bf \u001b(B\u001b[m"]
