[0.002, "o", "\u001b[32;1H\u001b[38;5;248m\u001b[48;5;255m\u276f \u001b[38;5;16mOK lots of questions and things to try:\u001b[39m                                                                               \u001b[33;1H                                                                                                                        \u001b[34;1H  \u001b[38;5;16m- Can we detect when mistral is likely to do badly and kick out to a better model?\u001b[39m                                    \u001b[35;1H  \u001b[38;5;16m- Is it just sequence mismatch or is mistral also actually bad? (Can we do set difference?)\u001b[39m                           \u001b[36;3H\u001b[49m \u001b[C  \u001b[C  \u001b[C    \u001b[C        \u001b[C        \u001b[C  \u001b[C  \u001b[C       \u001b[C    \u001b[C        \u001b[C    \u001b[C    \u001b[C  \u001b[C  \u001b[C   \u001b[C            \r\n\u001b[38;5;174m\u2736\u001b[CSwirling\u2026 \r\n\u001b[39m                                                                                                                        \u001b[39;1H\u001b[38;5;246m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
